=== Feir`Dal Fletching Kit (up to 163) ===
If you are not agro to Wood Elves, I would highly recommend making [[Feir`Dal Fletching Kit]]s up to 163.  This costs about 7pp per combine and will take you higher than Ornate Chain.  Don't be like me and burn 3000pp just to get to 133. I could have probably gotten to 163 for less than 2000pp if I had started with the kits.

You do NOT have to be a Wood Elf to use the Feir`Dal Forge or make Feir`Dal cultural crafting.

If you can't go to Kelethin, Ornate (below) is going to be your best bet. But just know it's really annoying to get materials for, and extremely expensive.

=== Ornate Chain (up to 142) ===
[[Ornate Chain Armor]] can get you to 142. It requires [[High Quality Metal Rings]] which are made from [[Large Brick of High Quality Ore]] which are a pain to get. You can sometimes find them on merchants that players sold to, along with [[Small Brick of High Quality Ore]] which can be turned into the Large Bricks. These are all extremely expensive - about 60pp for a single brick which will make 2 rings, if you don't fail.

So far the only merchant confirmed to always sell these in EQ Legends is [[Greta Terrilon]] in [[Halas]]. Unfortunately, no one in Halas seems to sell silver bars.

From the looks of it, the best path to 142 is:

* [[Ornate Chain Bracelet]] to 122 (~32pp per combine)
* [[Ornate Chain Coif]] to 132  (~65pp per combine)
* [[Ornate Chain Mail]] to 142  (~98pp per combine)

I spent about 3000pp on Ore, Silver Bars, and Patterns. It got me to 133 skill.

=== Fine Plate (up to 188) ===
* '''142 to 168:''' [[Fine Plate Bracer]]
* '''168 to 179:''' [[Fine Plate Helm]]
* '''179 to 188:''' [[Fine Plate Breastplate]]

== Skilling up Recommendations ==
The following recommendations are designed to strike a solid balance between saving time and saving money.

=== Basics ===

* Bypass [[Scaler]] in favor of [[Studs]], and then on to [[Skewers]]. This path avoids making multiple trips between merchants for molds <s>and eventually bottles</s> because you only require [[Metal Bits]] and [[Water Flask]] until you hit [[Skewers]] (which still use the supply of bits you will have acquired, as well as a single mold), but will cost a little more. Total cost to get from 1 to 100 skill (only 1 point put into it) using this method was approximately 100 plat (50 CHA, 161 WIS). '''~~NOTE~~''': Studs are trivial at 41, so you still need to do Large Lanterns (or similar i.e. Forged Javelins). Studs are a good stand-in for Scaler, though. 

* You CAN bypass ornate chain armors in favor of fine plate, or alternate between ornate and fine plate visors as you get in supplies for either. Getting your tailoring skills up high enough to make your own leather padding will save lots of money in the long run, and people often have silks and skins to sell-you can also reliable farm your own in newbie zones (There's a decent spot in Eastern Commons near the tunnel to farm spiderlings and random bear/wolf/cat skins for padding while you buy/sell with players). By making your own leather padding and selling your wares to merchants (if you can't find buyers), you will make back most of what you spend. Ornate chain requires more trips between the farming locale and bank/forge, but may be cheaper overall.

=== Banded ===

* For banded armor, Banded mask trivial 90, Banded Gorget (92), Banded Belt, boots, bracer or Mantle (95), Banded Cloak, Gauntlets, Helm or Sleeves (102), banded Leggings (108) and finally banded Mail at 115.

All Banded combines require a mold, water flask and some number of pieces of sheet metal. I would suggest gorget (1 piece sheet metal), any of gauntlets sleeve or cloak (all require 2 sheet metal), Helm (2 pieces sheet metal, then mail (requires 3 pieces of sheet metal)

* When working on banded armor, work in [[East Freeport]], [[Toxxulia Forest]], [[Qeynos Hills]], [[Greater Faydark]], or [[East Cabilis]]. These areas have [[Sheet Metal]] pre-made, which reduces your time spent as well as your losses due to sub-combine failure. I suggest Greater Faydark or East Freeport for most people. Trolls, Ogres, and Dark Elves have nowhere to buy it and must make their own.'''

=== Ornate Chain (Mantle, Boots, or Gloves) ===
* Banded covers you to 115 but there is a path to go from 175 -182 where you can make Ornate Chain.  

* It takes about 40-55 attempts with a HE Cleric having 198 WIS to go from 175 to 182 trivial.

*Ornate Chain is made with an unenchanted silver bar and High Quality Ore dropped by goblins in SolA or Permafrost and maybe Runnyeye. 

* It is easiest to farm SolA. Why SolA? There is a Gnome vendor (if you aren't KOS) in zone you can sell FS weapons and gems that drop off the goblins so you don't have to leave the zone.  If you can do the tricks to sell to the [[Goblin Merchant]] that is an option too.  Often either/both merchants will have HQ ore you can buy if you just want to spend the plat.  This is handy after making good coin selling FS weapons, gems, and jewelry the goblins like to drop.

* This takes time but may be less time and money than getting materials and beginning Fine Plate before you absolutely must do plate.

* The vendor in Freeport listed to sell the medium sized chain mold patterns does not exist at this time, use a different city. Felwithe and Neriak are good options because they sell patterns and silver bars.

* the HQ ore can frequently be found on merchants in Highkeep, and there is a forge in Highpass Hold just outside of Highkeep and to the left.

* High Quality Rings are not stackable, and 1 large brick of HQ ore turns in to 2 rings, so plan your bag space around this.  A good option is to pre purchase the stackable silver bars and patterns and convert bricks and immediately use the 2 rings to make an attempt at a mantle.

=== Fine Plate ===
* When working on fine plate armor, work in [[Highkeep]], or [[Qeynos]]. These are the only three cities where both the molds, AND the medium quality ores can be bought for 20pp each.
* Folded MQ sheets are stackable
* Get stacks and stacks and stacks of spiderling silks and make stacks and stacks of silk thread.  This is the most difficult part of doing fine steel besides having a couple thousand platinum to hit it hard (which you don't burn through too fast with reselling to vendor what you make, it just takes a good chunk of plat to start with).
* Once you have stacks and stacks and stacks (12-20 stacks) of [[Silk Thread]] made from spiderling silks take a [[Large Sewing Kit]], a [[Skinning Knife]], and all your stacks of silk thread to [[Stonebrunt Mountains]] to farm cat pelts.  The leopards almost always drop a LQ or MQ cat pelt.  You need the skinning knife to down grade MQ pelts to LQ.  Out of 200 pelts I just farmed I received 5 HQ pelts so don't expect many HQ if needing for other purposes.  As you get a pelt immediately turn it into stackable [[Leather Padding]].  Why do it this way?  Stonebrunt is far from everything and the pelts drop on almost every kill but do not stack.  It is only efficient to go here if you bring everything to convert the pelts into leather padding so you can walk in with stacks of silk thread and walk out with stacks of leather padding for fine plate smithing.

